// Regression: the try/catch sugar's synthesized `__ok` / `__rest`
// bindings must not shadow user identifiers of the same name in
// the try/catch bodies or patterns. Here the user has an outer
// `new __ok, __rest, log in { ... }` and references both inside
// both branches -- if the desugarer emitted the plain `__ok` /
// `__rest`, the log messages would silently see the inner
// for-comprehension bindings (a bool and a list) instead of the
// intended outer names.
//
// The paired hand-written form is try_catch_hygiene_desugared.rho,
// which uses `__ok0` / `__rest0` for the synthetic bindings so the
// user's `__ok` / `__rest` remain accessible.
new __ok, __rest, fs, log in {
  try @[file] <- fs!openFile("path.txt") {
    log!("opened", file, __ok, __rest)
  }
  catch @[code, msg] {
    log!("error", code, msg, __ok, __rest)
  }
}
